{"_meta":{"source":"Yahoo Finance via yfinance (profile, statements, analyst estimates)","fetched_at":"2026-10-22T15:53:52+00:00","status":"ok","error":null,"last_success":"2026-10-22T15:53:52+00:00"},"data":{"profile":{"name":"AB Volvo (publ)","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Farm & Heavy Construction Machinery","country":"Sweden","city":"Gothenburg","website":"https://www.volvogroup.com","employees":89417,"summary":"AB Volvo (publ), together with its subsidiaries, manufactures and sells trucks, buses, construction equipment, and marine and industrial engines in Europe, North America, South America, Asia, Africa, and Oceania. The company operates through Industrial Operations - Trucks, Industrial Operations - Construction Equipment, Industrial Operations - Buses, Industrial Operations - Volvo Penta, Industrial Operations - Group Functions & Other, and Financial Services segments. The company offers heavy-duty trucks for long-haulage and construction work, and light-duty trucks for distribution purposes under the Volvo, Renault Trucks, Mack, Eicher, and Dongfeng Trucks brands; and city and intercity buses, coaches, and chassis under the Prevost and Volvo Bus brands. It also provides haulers, wheel loaders, excavators, road construction machines, and compact equipment under the Volvo, SDLG, and Rokbak brands. In addition, the company offers engines and power solutions for industrial off-highway applications and power generation, as well as for leisure boats, yachts, and commercial vessels under the Volvo Penta brand. Further, it provides customer support agreements, machine control systems, attachments, financing, and leasing; and insurance, rentals, spare parts, repairs, preventive maintenance, uptime and service agreements, and assistance services. It serves customers primarily in the transportation, infrastructure, construction, marine, industrial, and public transportation industries. The company offers its products and services through a network of dealers. AB Volvo (publ) was incorporated in 1915 and is headquartered in Gothenburg, Sweden.","exchange":"Stockholm","currency":"SEK","financial_currency":"SEK","summary_fr":"AB Volvo (publ), avec ses filiales, fabrique et vend des camions, des autobus, du matériel de construction et des moteurs marins et industriels en Europe, en Amérique du Nord, en Amérique du Sud, en Asie, en Afrique et en Océanie. La société exerce ses activités par l'intermédiaire des secteurs Exploitation industrielle - Camions, Exploitation industrielle - Équipements de construction, Exploitation industrielle - Bus, Exploitation industrielle - Volvo Penta, Exploitation industrielle - Fonctions de groupe et autres, et Services financiers. La société propose des camions lourds pour les longs-courriers et les travaux de construction, et des camions légers à des fins de distribution sous les marques Volvo, Renault Trucks, Mack, Eicher et Dongfeng Trucks; et des autobus, autocars et châssis urbains et interurbains sous les marques Prevost et Volvo Bus."},"valuation":{"market_cap_yahoo":632810307584,"shares_outstanding":1592708968,"trailing_pe":17.651731,"forward_pe":12.4979925,"price_to_book":3.58385,"ev_to_ebitda":15.406,"ev_to_revenue":1.835,"dividend_yield":0.026500002,"payout_ratio":0.48240003,"beta_yahoo":1.0},"targets":{"current_price":311.2,"mean":355.12286,"median":360.0,"high":450.0,"low":281.0,"n_analysts":21,"reco_mean":2.27273,"reco_key":"buy"},"calendar":{"earnings_dates":["2026-10-23"],"eps_avg":5.54603,"eps_low":5.21,"eps_high":5.77,"revenue_avg":125141733030,"ex_dividend":"2026-04-09","dividend_date":null},"holders":{"insiders_pct":0.0189,"institutions_pct":0.64027,"institutions_float_pct":0.65261,"institutions_n":478,"institutions":[{"name":"Atlas Capital Advisors Inc","pct":0.0,"shares":7847,"value":2441986,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0},{"name":"Minot Deblois Advisors LLC                          ","pct":0.0,"shares":3350,"value":1042520,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0},{"name":"Pacer Advi